	(descr "Alps Alpine SKTAAAE010 tact switch, 2.6 x 1.6 x 0.53 mm. Land pattern from the Alps Alpine SKTA series catalog design/datasheets/w4_alps_skta_catalog.pdf page 2, Drawing No.1: 'Land Dimensions' (outer span 3.2, inner span 2.1, overall height 1.3, gap 0.2: four lands 0.55 x 0.55 at +-1.325 and +-0.375 from the centre). Terminal numbers as Alps gives them in the 'Dimensions' view on the same page (seen from above): 1 top left, 2 top right, 3 bottom left, 4 bottom right; 'Circuit Diagram': terminals 1 and 3 are joined, 2 and 4 are joined, the contact is between the two pairs. Reflow profile: product specification slim_alps-skta-aaae010-orwin.pdf page 4 (peak 260 C max 3 s). Solder paste: an opening 1:1 (0.55 x 0.55) on every land of this footprint, layer F.Paste, for a 0.08 mm stencil (same page, item 10.2 (4); design/mfg/assembly/process.md sections P2 and P8 change C1). This variant has all four lands (centre switch SW2).")
